    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is a **derived** value on the owner response, so I implemented it the same way the existing derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `displayName`, `initials`) are done in this codebase \u2014 no controller logic, since `OwnerDto` is generated from OpenAPI and computed via MapStruct.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n\nThis computes `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, `BRONZE` otherwise. Because `namesakeCount` is persisted at create time (by the existing `CountNamesakes` step) and the mapper runs for both `RespondWithOwner` (GET) and `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (POST), the tier is correct on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads the tests exercise.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and the full test run reports `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
